@startuml
title Purchase Request Workflow — Orchestration with Human Approval
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam ArrowColor #326d91
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam titleFontColor #12395b
skinparam titleFontSize 16
skinparam titleFontStyle bold
skinparam sequence {
  ActorBackgroundColor #e9f1f6
  ActorBorderColor #1d567d
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #e9f1f6
  ParticipantBorderColor #1d567d
  ParticipantFontColor #12395b
  LifeLineBorderColor #9eabb7
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #f4f6f8
  DatabaseBackgroundColor #d7e6ef
  DatabaseBorderColor #1d567d
  GroupBackgroundColor #fdf3e0
  GroupBorderColor #c9a227
  GroupFontColor #5a4600
  DividerBackgroundColor #f4f6f8
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #fff8e7
  BorderColor #c9a227
  FontColor #5a4600
}
skinparam legend {
  BackgroundColor #f4f6f8
  BorderColor #9eabb7
  FontColor #17212b
}

actor Submitter
actor Approver
participant "HTTP boundary" as HTTP
participant "Request / approval services" as Service
participant "Execution coordinator" as Coordinator
participant "Orchestration strategy" as Orchestrator
participant "Shared step service" as Step
participant "Task executor" as Executor
participant "Retry policy + resolver" as Policy
participant "Unit of work" as UoW
database Database

Submitter -> HTTP : submit structured purchase data + revision + orchestration
HTTP -> Service : create submission
Service -> UoW : commit purchase request + run + READY cursor + trace
UoW -> Database : transaction
Database --> UoW : committed
Service -> Coordinator : drive(run identity)
Coordinator -> Orchestrator : execute from cursor

loop while cursor is READY
  Orchestrator -> Step : execute current task
  alt HUMAN_APPROVAL
    Step -> UoW : create/get work item; set purchase request/run WAITING; trace
    UoW -> Database : transaction
    Database --> UoW : committed
    Step --> Orchestrator : waiting
  else automatic task
    Step -> Executor : execute(context)
    Executor --> Step : TaskResult
    Step -> UoW : persist attempt/result
    UoW -> Database : transaction
    Database --> UoW : committed
    Step -> Policy : retry or resolve?
    alt retryable technical failure below bound
      Policy --> Step : retry same task; no edge
      Step -> UoW : persist retry + READY cursor
      UoW -> Database : transaction
      Database --> UoW : committed
    else final result
      Policy --> Step : transition or terminal
      Step -> UoW : persist next cursor or terminal + trace
      UoW -> Database : transaction
      Database --> UoW : committed
    end
  end
end

Coordinator --> Service : waiting or terminal projection
Service --> HTTP : purchase request/run status
HTTP --> Submitter : current result

opt run waits for approval
  Approver -> HTTP : approve or reject work item
  HTTP -> Service : decide once
  Service -> UoW : commit decision + purchase request outcome + READY cursor + trace
  UoW -> Database : transaction with decision uniqueness check
  Database --> UoW : committed or controlled conflict
  Service -> Coordinator : drive same run identity
  Coordinator -> Orchestrator : resume from persisted cursor
  Orchestrator -> Step : continue shared algorithm to terminal
  Step -> UoW : commit authorization/notification/terminal steps
  UoW -> Database : transactions
  Database --> UoW : committed
  Service --> HTTP : final purchase request/run projection
  HTTP --> Approver : authoritative decision result
end

legend
Central control stops at WAITING and returns; it never blocks for a person.
Business failure and rejection route without automatic retry.
Automated acceptance exercises the same waiting/resume sequence.
endlegend
@enduml
